exports[`explanation text for every example > union in generic: advanced 1`] = `
"Returns name and email from customers, combined with 1 more query (UNION), sorted by name.
FROM: Picks where the rows come from.
SELECT: Works out the output columns.
UNION: Combines the results of the queries into one result; each must return the same number of columns.
  + UNION removes duplicate rows; UNION ALL keeps them and does less work.
  + The result's column names come from the first query.
  + INTERSECT is evaluated before UNION and EXCEPT. ORDER BY and the row limit apply to the combined result.
ORDER BY: Sorts the final result.
  + Rows with equal sort values can come back in any order; a unique column (such as id) as the last sort key makes the order stable.
  + Where NULLs sort depends on the database. Some accept NULLS FIRST or NULLS LAST; sorting on a CASE works everywhere."
`;

