VALUES: The rows you typed, one new row each.
  + Columns that aren't listed get their default value, or NULL.
INSERT INTO: Adds the rows to the table.
  + If any row breaks a constraint (a unique key, NOT NULL or a foreign key), the statement fails and no rows are added.
ON CONFLICT: When a row clashes with an existing unique key, this decides what happens instead of an error.
  + ON CONFLICT needs a unique index or constraint on the conflict columns. EXCLUDED is the row that was about to be inserted."
`;

