exports[`explanation text for every example > window in generic: advanced 1`] = `
"Returns name, department, salary and 2 more columns from employees.
FROM: Picks where the rows come from.
SELECT: Works out the output columns. Window functions (RANK, SUM) are calculated over the remaining rows without merging them.
  + running_payroll uses the rows from the start of its partition to the current row (a running value).
  + Window functions run after WHERE, GROUP BY and HAVING, so they can't be filtered there; put this query in a CTE and filter the outer query."
`;

